-- Row il-69. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: two items (I1 and I2), the provisions they name (statuses as the instruments read give them), and the control beside I2 (the next paragraph of the same subsection).
-- The later instruments read (limb (b)) are typed below, before the items. Tests of the controls are in jt69-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in jt69-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (three: two for I1, one for I2) are in jt69-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[shNNNN-pPPP]` and `ext:[kt7445-pPPP]` lines quote the Hebrew read from the deposited page image of Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNNN, or of Kovetz HaTakanot (KT) issue 7445, printed page PPP (registers/source-bundle/pages/). They are the printed instruments.
-- The Hebrew on those lines was copied mechanically (a script copies each string from the row's written source, and each was compared with the text layer of the page and with the deposited crop; NOTES.md says which comparisons were made and which could not be).
-- The Hebrew inside the lists of words below is generated from the same quotation strings. Nothing is typed from memory.
-- Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.

§ `References`

